# A Plug and Play mouse follows its "M" with its identity between
# parentheses, "(MSH0001)" here; its letters would begin packets and move
# the mouse. The driver passes over it: only the packet after counts
# (mouse, roadmap os-server.md P12).
program: sh
install: C /BIN/MOUSE z-mouse.rx
keys: {wait 20}{mouse-bytes 28 4D 53}{mouse-bytes 48 30 30}{mouse-bytes 30 31 29}mouse\n{wait 5}{mouse 8 0 -}{wait 2}{mouse 0 0 LR}
---
rx286, test build
/mnt/rx286$ mouse
Move the mouse; Esc or both buttons end.
x 320, y 100 (column 40, row 12), buttons: none
x 328, y 100 (column 41, row 12), buttons: none
x 328, y 100 (column 41, row 12), buttons: both
/mnt/rx286$
